    <note type="translation" xml:lang="en">Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad, originally from Yemen, then from Rūm (Anatolia) and Bursa, then a resident of Cairo, settled in al-Shaykhūniyya, and was known as Ibn ʿArab. He is mentioned in the biography of those whose grandfather was Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿArab.</note>
